<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss pharmaceutical exports rise in 1995.</title>
<headline>Swiss pharmaceutical exports rise in 1995.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss pharmaceutical exports rose to 12.43 billion Swiss francs in 1995 as the country's trade surplus in such products widened, Pharma Information said.</p>
<p>(in millions of Swiss francs)</p>
<p>					   1995		   1994</p>
<p> Exports				12,430		 11,795</p>
<p> Imports				 4,020		  3,795</p>
<p> Balance				 8,410		  8,000</p>
<p>Pharma Information is operated jointly by Ciba-Geigy AG, Roche Holding AG and Sandoz AG.</p>
<p>The companies together account for 90 percent of Swiss pharmaceutical exports and posted 23.2 billion francs in global pharmaceutical sales last year.</p>
<p>It said pharmaceuticals made up 52 percent of the total Swiss chemical exports and 13 percent of overall exports.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
